                <pb facs="0227" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg93"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 749.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Contract between the Guatemalan Government and John T.
                        Anderson—Northern Railway of Guatemala.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article IX.</hi></p>
                <p>The enterprise, with the exception of Chinese, has the right to import the number
                    of workmen it may need, and the government will employ all means in its power to
                    enforce the contracts they make with the enterprise; said contracts will be
                    considered valid in the republic, although celebrated in a foreign country; this
                    will be consigned in the respective contracts.</p>
            </div>
